  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "Fashion follows trends but it generally is more revealing and sexual than Old Money styles. Local culture can drastically change fashion aesthetics - parts of California have a more bohemian vibe while Manhattan tends to be more Chic Modernist.",
    "Gold and Jet Set": "Visible brand names and logos; Dresses with plunging necklines and high slit skirts; Skimpy bikinis; Shirts worn open on men; Sequins and metallic fabrics; Fur coats; Designer sneakers and athleisure; Extremely high heels",
    "Bourgeois Bohemian": "Light airy garments made from organic cotton, linen, and silk; Kaftans; Muumuus; Sandals; Espadrilles; Light wash denim jeans and shorts",
    "Minimalist": "More gender neutral and androgynous; Color palette consisting of black, gray, white, and tan; Simplistic patterns and graphics",
    "Gold Makeup": "Metallic lipstick, eyeshadow, and nail polish",
    "Jet Set Makeup": "Long \"coffin\" nails; Heavy contouring; Dark fake tan; Brightly colored lipstick, eyeshadow, and nail polish; Fake eyelashes",
    "Bourgeois Bohemian Makeup": "Natural makeup or none worn at all; Organically produced products",
    "Minimalist Makeup": "Bold red lipstick; Darkened eyebrows"
  },
